{
  "id": "queue-kanji-backfill-share",
  "title": "Backfill kanji take at most half the daily new goal; new words get the rest; the remaining kanji come on the next study day (ADR-044)",
  "covers": [
    "queue.kanji_backfill_share"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "new_per_day is 4, so the backfill share is floor(4 / 2) = 2. 日本語 (card ...10) was graduated two days ago with Easy (review state, not due); its kanji notes 日 (card ...40), 本 (card ...50) and 語 (card ...60) exist and are new: three backfill kanji. The deck \"Words\" holds two new kana words, うっかり (card ...20) then Ｔシャツ (card ...30).",
    "Step 0: backfill draws 日 and 本 (2 of 2) and stops at 語; the deck then draws うっかり and Ｔシャツ; the goal of 4 is full, so 語 is not served. The three kanji cards are deckless, but a backfill kanji has no turn of its own in the deckless source, so 語 does not take a slot there either. until_stop is 4.",
    "Steps 1-2 introduce 日 and 本 (Easy). Step 3: both count as today's backfill (日本語 was introduced on an earlier day), the share is used up, so the rebuild serves only the two words and still not 語. until_stop is 2.",
    "Steps 4-5 introduce the two words. Step 6: the goal is reached exactly (4/4): done_for_today, until_stop 0; 語 is still new, so new.available is true.",
    "Step 7, the next study day (04:00:01Z): 語 is served (1 of the share of 2); nothing else is new. until_stop is 1."
  ],
